<title>MALAYSIA: Bank Negara's reserves rise to 70.71 bln ringgit.</title>
<headline>Bank Negara's reserves rise to 70.71 bln ringgit.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Negara's gold, foreign exchange and other reserves rose to 70.71 billion ringgit as at June 30 against 70.15 billion a fortnight earlier, the Bank said in a statement. </p>
<p>The central bank said its total assets and liabilities rose to 100.99 billion ringgit from 96.72 billion two weeks earlier.</p>
<p>(In bln ringgit)  June 30 1997    June 14 1997    June 29 1996</p>
<p>Reserves		 70.71	     70.15	     66.87</p>
<p>Assets		  100.99	     96.72	     95.92</p>
<p>Currency		 21.95	     22.30	     19.44</p>
<p>Govt paper		1.74		1.90		3.40</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
